@page
@model Aibysitter.Web.Pages.Rules.IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Rules";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Every aibysitter lint rule and pull request check: what each flags, with before and after examples.";
}

<h1>Rules</h1>

<h2>Rules files</h2>
<p>Checked by the <a asp-page="/Lint">lint page</a> against CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, Cursor rules (.mdc and .cursorrules), Copilot instructions, GEMINI.md, and .windsurfrules. Frontmatter is skipped by every rule except R009, R015 and R016. R015 and R016 apply to Cursor .mdc rules only.</p>
<partial name="_RulesTable" model="Model.Rows" />
<p><a asp-page="/Rules/Methodology">How rules are chosen and scored</a> · <a asp-page="/Rules/Changelog">Changelog (ruleset v@(Aibysitter.Rules.RulesetVersion.Current))</a></p>

<h2>Aibysitter lint score</h2>
<partial name="_Scoring" />
<p>Fenced code blocks are excluded from all rules. Headings are excluded from R001–R003.</p>

<h2>Suppressing a rule</h2>
<p>An HTML comment on its own line. IDs are required; separate several with commas. Suppressed findings are listed on the lint page and not scored.</p>
<p>Suppression comments live in the rules file itself: the agent reads them and they cost tokens on every run. For the GitHub App, prefer <code>disable</code> in <code>.github/aibysitter.json</code>.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;!-- aibysitter-disable R002 --&gt;            whole file
&lt;!-- aibysitter-disable-next-line R001, R005 --&gt;   the next line only</code></pre>

<h2>Pull request checks</h2>
<p>Run by the <a asp-page="/GitHub">GitHub App</a> on every pull request in an installed repository.</p>
<partial name="_RulesTable" model="Model.CheckRows" />
